    <briefdescription>
<para>RAII lease of a single pooled <ref refid="classDatabase" kindref="compound">Database</ref> connection. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The constructor leases a connection from a <ref refid="classDatabaseConnectionPool" kindref="compound">DatabaseConnectionPool</ref> (waiting up to the acquire timeout and possibly throwing <ref refid="classDatabaseBusy" kindref="compound">DatabaseBusy</ref>); the destructor returns it, so a thrown query exception cannot leak the connection. Intended as a short-lived, stack-allocated helper (the watchdog and controllers create one per check/query). Non-copyable and non-movable: one lease, one connection. <simplesect kind="note"><para>The class name is spelled <computeroutput><ref refid="classDatabaseHanndler" kindref="compound">DatabaseHanndler</ref></computeroutput> as used throughout the codebase. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classDatabaseConnectionPool" kindref="compound">DatabaseConnectionPool</ref>, <ref refid="classDatabaseBusy" kindref="compound">DatabaseBusy</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
